<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">French Cochinchina</h1><p class="st-meta">1862 CE – 1949 CE · capital Saigon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southern third of Vietnam, ruled directly by France as a colony from the 1860s, with Saigon as its capital and rice and rubber as its wealth.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-nang">Da Nang</a> in 1858 and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> in 1859. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862">Treaty of Saigon</a> in 1862 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tu-duc">Emperor Tu Duc</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty">Nguyen dynasty</a> ceded three eastern provinces, and in 1867 Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pierre-paul-de-la-grandiere">de La Grandiere</a> seized the three western ones, completing the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nguyen-lords">Cochinchina</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Unlike the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-annam">Annam</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-tonkin">Tonkin</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nguyen-lords">Cochinchina</a> was a full colony under French law, with an elected colonial council and a deputy in the French parliament. Canals and drainage opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> delta to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> exports, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> plantations spread in the east. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cholon">Cholon</a> grew into a major port with large Chinese communities. Religious movements such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caodaism">Cao Dai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-hao">Hoa Hao</a> arose.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> set up the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/autonomous-republic-of-cochinchina">Autonomous Republic of Cochinchina</a> in 1946. In 1949 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nguyen-lords">Cochinchina</a> was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-vietnam">State of Vietnam</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a>, ending its separate status.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-cochinchina.jpg" alt="French Cochinchina" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1862 CE – 1949 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Saigon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pierre-Paul de La Grandiere</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Catholicism, Cao Dai</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cochinchina, Colony of Cochinchina, Nam Kỳ</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=french-cochinchina" aria-label="French Cochinchina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7619 1775 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Cochinchina lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7939 2031L7930 1822M7939 2031L5054 728M7939 2031L7939 2031M7939 2031L7939 2031M7939 2031L7939 2031"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7930 1822h0M5054 728h0M7939 2031h0M7939 2031h0M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7939 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M